Extensible Computational Chemistry Environment (ECCE)

Environmental Molecular Sciences Laboratory (EMSL)
Pacific Northwest National Laboratory
Richland, WA 99352

ECCE is an open-source suite of integrated collaborative applications for
setting up, running, and visualizing results from computational chemistry
studies distributed under the terms of the Educational Community License
(ECL) 2.0

Copyright (c) 1994-2012 Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, Battelle
Memorial Institute.

Copyright (c) 2017-2026 CA Ohlin.

This distribution is a maintained fork, hosted at
https://github.com/FriendsofECCE/ECCE. The software has been substantially
modified since 2012 -- ported from wxWidgets 2.8 to 3.2, from C++14 to C++17,
from a recursive-make build to CMake, and from Python 2 to Python 3, with
extensive bug fixes and support for additional computational chemistry codes.
Neither Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, Battelle Memorial Institute nor
the U.S. Department of Energy is responsible for, or endorses, these
modifications.

This software and its documentation were originally developed at the EMSL at
Pacific Northwest National Laboratory, a multiprogram national laboratory,
operated for the U.S. Department of Energy by Battelle under Contract Number
DE-AC05-76RL01830. Support for that work was provided by the Department of
Energy Office of Biological and Environmental Research, Office of Basic
Energy Sciences.

